  <content>
  <section><title>Warm Up Activity</title>
<para><figure><media alt="a drone flying"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/3549f9fb392a0a4dd582f0fe064c6c89e01646bb"/></media></figure></para>

<para>Here is a graph that represents function \(f\), which gives the height of a drone, in meters, \(t\) seconds after it leaves the ground.</para>
<para><figure><media alt="Graph. Horizontal axis, 0 to 8, time, seconds. Vertical axis, height, meters. Starting at 0 comma 0, the graph increases linearly. From 2 to 6, it’s horizontal. Then decreases linearly to 7 comma 0."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/3192aada43883aac8e77e8ee8af08927d79ed818"/></media></figure></para>

<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="84f7b988-8fdf-48f1-9ef4-5088bcd2bc2e" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <exercise data-content-id="19dfec9e-2568-4884-8040-50c90159ae7d" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-solution="f(4)" data-solution-options="[&quot;f(0)&quot;, &quot;f(4)&quot;,&quot;They are equal.&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> Decide which function value is greater.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(f(4)\) </para>
    </solution>

    </exercise>
  <!--Do not edit below this line-->
  <solution> </solution>
  </div>
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Explain your thinking:</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer: Your answer may vary, but here is a sample. 
      The output value at f(4) is greater than the output value at f(0) because at 4 seconds the drone is 4 meters off the ground while at 0 seconds, the drone is on the ground (0 meters).</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="fea0f009-b451-43c3-a656-f12455ee8d1b" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <exercise data-content-id="9686b5e5-9081-4c5f-9c48-bc94d43a66a3" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-solution="They are equal." data-solution-options="[&quot;f(2)&quot;, &quot;f(5)&quot;, &quot;They are equal.&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> Decide which function value is greater.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! They are equal.</para>
    </solution>
        </exercise>
  <!--Do not edit below this line-->
  <solution> </solution>
  </div>
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Explain your thinking:</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer: Your answer may vary, but here is a sample. 
      The output value at f(2) is equal to the output value at f(5) because at both 2 seconds and 5 seconds, the drone is 4 meters off the ground.</para>
  </solution></exercise>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="b9c141b4-2fe2-4c93-a82f-9dd8a42ff3c8" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <exercise data-content-id="fed73eb3-63f0-418a-aa1e-14cfa827d1d4" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-solution="f(3)" data-solution-options="[&quot;f(3)&quot;, &quot;f(7)&quot;, &quot;They are equal.&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> Decide which function value is greater.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(f(3)\)</para>
    </solution>
        </exercise>
  <!--Do not edit below this line-->
  <solution> </solution>
  </div>
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Explain your thinking:</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer: Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.
      The output value at f(3) is greater than the output value at f(7) because at 3 seconds the drone is 4 meters off the ground while at 7 seconds, the drone is on the ground (0 meters).</para>
  </solution></exercise>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="5d36581e-df63-4394-9d81-41880f5390ea" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <exercise data-content-id="9e277471-1208-4272-90cd-87faf11ca143" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-solution="It depends on the value of \\(t\\)." data-solution-options="[&quot;f(t)&quot;, &quot;f(t+1)&quot;, &quot;They are equal.&quot;, &quot;It depends on the value of t.&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> Decide which function value is greater.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! It depends on the value of \(t\).</para>
    </solution>
        </exercise>
  <!--Do not edit below this line-->
  <solution> </solution>
  </div>
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Explain your thinking:</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer: Your answer may vary, but here are some samples. 
    </para><list>
      <item>It depends on the value of t because during some time periods the values of the function are equal. </item>
      <item>It depends on the value of t because between 0-2 seconds, f(t+1) is greater than f(t) but it is exactly the opposite between 5-7 seconds where f(t) is greater.</item>
      <item>It depends on the value of t because between 0-2 seconds, f(t+1) is greater, between 2-5 seconds the values are equal, and after 5 seconds, f(t) is greater.</item>
    </list>
    
  </solution></exercise>

